<title>USA: Trend-Lines to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Trend-Lines to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>REVERE, Mass. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trend-Lines Inc said on Tuesday its board had authorized the repurchase of up to 500,000 shares.</p>
<p>The company said it has about 11 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Trend-Lines, a specialty retailer of woodworking tools and accessories, recently named Richard Griner, a former Family Dollar Stores Inc executive, as president.</p>
<p>Griner succeeded Stanley Black, who remained Trend-Lines chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
